== 4. Framework Timing Predictions
<framework-timing-predictions>
=== 4.1 Methodology
<methodology>
Applying the Atlas computational framework to tin operations: tin is
single-graha (Guru) for the primary substance, with co-substance
contributions varying by procedure.

=== 4.2 Pure tin operations (shodhana, jarana, simple bhasma)
<pure-tin-operations-shodhana-jarana-simple-bhasma>
Single-graha analysis (Guru-only). Friendship from BPHS: - Guru is
friend of: Surya (Sun), Chandra (Moon), Mangala (Mars) - Guru is enemy
of: Budha (Mercury), Shukra (Venus) - Guru is neutral to: Shani
(Saturn), Rahu, Ketu

Framework predicts: - #strong[Most favorable]: Krittika, Uttara
Phalguni, Uttara Ashadha (Surya-ruled, Surya-Guru friend); Rohini,
Hasta, Shravana (Chandra-ruled, Chandra-Guru friend); Mrigashira,
Chitra, Dhanishtha (Mangala-ruled, Mangala-Guru friend); Punarvasu,
Vishakha, Purva Bhadrapada (Guru-ruled, own-graha) - #strong[Strong]:
Pushya, Anuradha, Uttara Bhadrapada (Shani-ruled, neutral); Ardra,
Swati, Shatabhisha (Rahu-ruled, neutral) - #strong[Avoid]: Aslesha,
Jyeshtha, Revati (Budha-ruled — Budha enemy of Guru); Bharani, Purva
Phalguni, Purva Ashadha (Shukra-ruled — Shukra enemy of Guru)

Tin’s friendship pattern is favorable across many nakshatras (Guru
friend of three grahas), though the dual enmity with Budha and Shukra
creates some restricted windows. This pattern is more flexible than
iron’s (Shani has three enmities) but more restricted than silver’s
(Chandra has zero enmities).

=== 4.3 Tin-mercury operations (when mercury-mediated route is used)
<tin-mercury-operations-when-mercury-mediated-route-is-used>
Two-graha (Guru + Budha). Guru-Budha is #emph[enemy] both directions.
This creates significant timing tension.

Framework predicts: - #strong[Most favorable]: Pushya, Anuradha, Uttara
Bhadrapada (Shani-ruled — neutral to both grahas; Dhruva activity-class
adds bonus) - #strong[Strong secondary]: Ardra, Swati, Shatabhisha
(Rahu-ruled — neutral to both) - #strong[Avoid]: nakshatras of grahas
friendly to one and unfriendly to the other (creates contradictions)

This is one of the most timing-sensitive operations in the dhatu
compendium because of the strong Guru-Budha enmity. The
Pushya-as-stable-anchor pattern continues from previous volumes.

=== 4.4 Tin-mercury-sulfur operations (vanga-sindhura, mercury-mediated
vanga-bhasma)
<tin-mercury-sulfur-operations-vanga-sindhura-mercury-mediated-vanga-bhasma>
Three-graha (Guru + Budha + Mangala). Guru-Budha is enemy; Guru-Mangala
